[h2]🔗 Load order with other mods[/h2]
In the Paradox Launcher the mod [b]lower[/b] in the playset loads later and wins any file both mods change.
[table]
[tr][th]Mod[/th][th]Order[/th][th]Notes[/th][/tr]
[tr][td][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2777392649]Millennium Dawn[/url][/td][td]MD above, FPS Map below[/td][td]Tested with 2.0.3.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3826896215]Millennium Dawn +Turkey[/url][/td][td]Any order[/td][td]Checked: shares no files with FPS Map.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3350890356]The Fire Rises[/url][/td][td]Works[/td][td]Tested, no problems.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3816496697]Globe Mod[/url][/td][td]✖ Not compatible[/td][td]Unfortunately incompatible: both mods replace the same map shaders, and the map does not turn into a globe when they are combined. Load order does not help.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Original FPS Map (Mlecz)[/td][td]✖ Disable it[/td][td]Same files; this mod replaces it.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]UI, unit, flag, focus and overhaul mods[/td][td]Any order[/td][td]Checked: Historical Army Insignia and Focus Tree Swapper share no files; Hearts of Iron: 1984 Revived shares 3 icons (the lower mod's icon art shows).[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Other shader / map-graphics mods[/td][td]Your choice[/td][td]If both change the same file, the lower mod wins that file; the rest of FPS Map still applies.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Why is it Ironman & MP safe?[/b] The game checksum only covers [i]common/, events/, history/[/i] and map data files. This mod touches none of them — only shaders, textures and arrow visuals — so your checksum stays identical to vanilla (verified in game).

[hr][/hr]

[h2]🛠 What was fixed compared to the original[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Crash / broken arrows fixed:[/b] the map-arrow shader was an outdated copy missing three effects the engine now requires (raid arrows, see-through plan arrows). Rebuilt from the 1.20 shader with the mod's style re-applied.
[*][b]HQ / general connection lines restored:[/b] 12 arrow and symbol types added in recent patches (deployed-general front lines, commander ability range, raid arrows) were missing and simply did not draw.
[*][b]Invalid reflection texture replaced:[/b] the water/sky reflection was a flat image where the game expects a cube map. Now a proper (black) cube map — same look, no rendering errors.
[*][b]Cleanup:[/b] 15 obsolete or unused files removed.
[/list]
Every changed file is rebuilt from the [i]current[/i] vanilla file with only the mod's own edits applied, so nothing new from Paradox is lost.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]📦 Installation[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]In the Paradox Launcher, add [b]FPS Map - Vanilla Icons (Ironman & MP Safe)[/b] to your playset.
[*][b]Disable the original FPS Map[/b] if you have it — both replace the same files.
[/olist]

[h2]❓ FAQ[/h2]
[b]Will it really raise my FPS?[/b]
No. This is a visual clean-up (calmer water, flat arrows, softer weather), not an FPS booster. It trims a little shader work on water, rivers and arrows, but not enough to expect a noticeable difference. Late-game slowdowns come from the game simulation on the CPU, which no map mod can fix.

[b]Does it change gameplay?[/b]
No. Purely visual.

[b]Can I use it with other UI / map mods?[/b]
Yes — see the load order guide above. Put the mod you want to win lower in the playset.

[b]Sea and land regions show names like "STRATEGICREGION_49" — is this mod broken?[/b]
No — FPS Map ships no text. The debug map editor (Nudger) left files in your user folder that override every mod. Move the contents of the [i]localisation[/i] and [i]map[/i] folders in [i]Documents/Paradox Interactive/Hearts of Iron IV/[/i] somewhere else (keep a copy). A leftover [i]map/unitstacks.txt[/i] there also changes your checksum and blocks Ironman achievements.

Found a bug? Leave a comment with your game version, DLC list and your [i]Documents/Paradox Interactive/Hearts of Iron IV/logs/error.log[/i].
